It's not an actual drug unit? I don't know...

00:11:05.560 --> 00:11:11.280
But you know what, we're not done yet! Because we have not even addressed the biggest issue that Wakanda isn't even thinking about here

00:11:11.280 --> 00:11:14.900
When the world has something that scarce, what usually happens?

00:11:14.940 --> 00:11:16.960
Do we usually just use it all up and say

00:11:16.960 --> 00:11:22.040
"Well that was fun was fun while it lasted. That oil phase that was a really cool phase wasn't it?"

00:11:22.040 --> 00:11:27.000
Not really, when there's a scarcity of a resource, prices go up, that's called supply and demand.

00:11:27.700 --> 00:11:30.920
If the price gets too high people are like:

00:11:30.920 --> 00:11:32.980
"Eh I'm going to use less of this to save money.

00:11:32.980 --> 00:11:37.580
Or maybe i'll stop using it all together and figure out something to replace this thing."

00:11:37.580 --> 00:11:41.140
It's especially that last part that Wakanda has to worry about, here.

00:11:41.780 --> 00:11:44.100
Just look at history to tell you why.

00:11:44.100 --> 00:11:47.220
Back in the 1800s, everyone used to use whale oil in their lamps,

00:11:47.220 --> 00:11:53.660
Besides being really tragic and sad, it also started to get really expensive when whales, you know, started to go extinct

00:11:53.660 --> 00:11:57.380
Like I said, this whole thing is really sad, but, go figure, it gets better.

00:11:57.380 --> 00:12:03.520
Whale oil became so rare that people couldn't afford it anymore, so they started finding alternatives,

00:12:03.520 --> 00:12:05.820
Specifically switching to Kerosene.

00:12:05.820 --> 00:12:09.880
At the time crude oil, was just this sludge, which farmers that getting annoyed by, in Texas

00:12:09.880 --> 00:12:15.880
But people realized it would burn better than whale oil and, go figure, it was a heck of a lot cheaper.

00:12:15.900 --> 00:12:20.000
So they switched, when the oil tycoons came along oil got even cheaper,

00:12:20.100 --> 00:12:24.720
And then, all of a sudden, people could heat their houses, run cars, and finally leave the whales alone.

00:12:24.920 --> 00:12:31.880
Not because they were super nice or Because whales are majestic, but because they found a better, cheaper alternative.

00:12:31.880 --> 00:12:36.100
TLDR: John D. Rockefeller saved the whales. No joke.

00:12:36.100 --> 00:12:38.900
For a more close to home example: For all of us, on the Internet though,

00:12:38.900 --> 00:12:41.980
You ever wonder where fiber optic cable came from?

00:12:42.140 --> 00:12:45.220
As early as the 1980s, copper became scarce.

00:12:45.360 --> 00:12:49.040
But the demand for copper wiring for phones and electricity was huge.

00:12:49.040 --> 00:12:58.920
So instead of paying super high copper prices, people started to look For cheaper, more effective, ways to deliver cable, and discovered fiber optics.

00:12:59.100 --> 00:13:03.860
Fiber optics cables are literally made of sand which there is no shortage of.

00:13:03.860 --> 00:13:09.680
Actually delivers better signals than copper ever did, and happens to be dirt cheap, literally.

00:13:09.680 --> 00:13:12.720
The point of these examples is that when resources are too expensive,

00:13:12.720 --> 00:13:17.100
People don't just sit around and wait for the next time, some greedy country wants to sell some off.

00:13:17.100 --> 00:13:17.700
No, sir.

00:13:17.700 --> 00:13:19.960
Instead they leave the counntry in the dust

00:13:19.960 --> 00:13:22.060
By developing an alternative.

