00:15:44.680 --> 00:15:48.320
That's entirely his right as the sole-decision maker for the country.

00:15:48.320 --> 00:15:53.340
It's a perfect demonstration of the challenges of a command and control economy that we talked about in this episode.

00:15:53.340 --> 00:16:00.200
One, or a small handful of people, can choose to do whatever they want with the sole resource everything the economy depends on.

00:16:00.200 --> 00:16:06.820
And, as we see in the movie, it prompts a literal civil war as they fight over what to do with the vibranium supply.

00:16:06.820 --> 00:16:09.820
Then, did y'all notice T'Challa's line about "the world catching up"?

00:16:09.820 --> 00:16:14.920
And how that makes it more critical for Wakanda to open its borders in terms of knowledge and technology?

00:16:14.920 --> 00:16:21.240
It's exactly what we said about vibranium making itself obsolete if the country isn't nicer to its potential trade partners.

00:16:21.240 --> 00:16:24.000
Which leads us to the conclusion to the entire film:

00:16:24.000 --> 00:16:27.440
Wakanda shows itself welcome to helping the rest of the world.

00:16:27.440 --> 00:16:31.240
Which is exactly the recommendation we made for it in the first place.

00:16:31.240 --> 00:16:35.200
The Wakandan economy has moved past how it was run by its ancestors,

00:16:35.200 --> 00:16:36.300
And it's evolved.

00:16:36.300 --> 00:16:39.840
And now, the country will be able to remain viable for years to come.

00:16:39.840 --> 00:16:43.100
So hey, it actually turned out to not really be a theory.

00:16:43.180 --> 00:16:45.180
